From: apklayer
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer: hwservicemanager as a shared library

Appends libapklayer_hwservicemanager: the binary's own sources (service.cpp with its main, ServiceManager, HidlService, Vintf, TokenManager) as a
shared library exporting main, because bionic_translation loads libraries, not executables (as frameworks/native 0004 does for servicemanager).
The SELinux access policy (AccessControl.cpp) is replaced by vendor/apklayer's allow-all one (aosp/hals/hwservicemanager). Rebuild:
`m libapklayer_hwservicemanager`. docs/HIDL.md.
Against system/hwservicemanager 60271965cf6b (REVISION). Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
---
diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -138,3 +138,23 @@ cc_test {
     ],
     test_suites: ["device-tests"],
 }
+
+// apklayer: the HIDL service manager as a library (its main() is exported) so a launcher on bionic_translation can run it.
+cc_library_shared {
+    name: "libapklayer_hwservicemanager",
+    defaults: [
+        "hwservicemanager_defaults",
+        "libhwservicemanager_shared_libs",
+        "libtokenmanager_shared_libs",
+    ],
+    srcs: [
+        "HidlService.cpp",
+        "ServiceManager.cpp",
+        "Vintf.cpp",
+        "TokenManager.cpp",
+        "service.cpp",
+        ":apklayer_hwservicemanager_access",
+    ],
+    shared_libs: ["libcutils"],
+    compile_multilib: "64",
+}
